From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Declare the build inputs and outputs gnrt cannot discover

gnrt builds a crate's `sources`/`inputs` lists by walking the directory that
holds its root source file. Three crates the `adblock` engine depends on read
or write files that walk does not reach, and each stops the build with a
different message.

    ERROR: Rust source file or input not in GN sources:
      .../vendor/cssparser-v0_29/build/match_byte.rs

    ERROR: Rust source file or input not in GN inputs:
      .../vendor/rmp-v0_8/README.md

    error: couldn't read out/GateCheck/gen/third_party/rust/selectors/v0_24/lib/
      ascii_case_insensitive_html_attributes.rs: No such file or directory

Three separate declarations because they are three separate mechanisms, all
of which `gnrt_config.toml` already has a key for -- upstream makes the same
declarations for `clap`, `image`, `prost`, `typed-path`, `read-fonts` and the
`icu_*_data` crates. Nothing here is novel; it is the paperwork a crate needs
when it is vendored for the first time.

cssparser 0.29.6, both directions at once
    `build.rs` declares `#[path = "build/match_byte.rs"] mod match_byte;`, so
    the module is a source of the BUILD SCRIPT, not of the library -- hence
    `extra_build_script_src_roots` rather than `extra_src_roots`. The path is
    resolved against the directory of the crate's root source file
    (`collect_crate_files` does `lib_root.join(path)` for every root), which
    is `src/`, so the entry is `'../build'` and not `'build'`.
    It then writes `$OUT_DIR/tokenizer.rs`, which `src/lib.rs:103` reads with
    `include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/tokenizer.rs"))`. That is the second
    declaration; without it the build script compiles, runs, and its output is
    discarded when `run_build_script.py` copies nothing out of the temp dir.
    The first failure hides the second, so both are fixed together rather
    than one per round trip.

rmp 0.8.15
    `src/lib.rs` line 1 is `#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`. A README
    is a compile input the moment a crate does that, and `rustc_wrapper.py`
    checks the depfile against the declared set. Note that a README reached
    only from a `#[cfg(doctest)]` item does NOT need this -- `hashbrown` in
    the same dependency set has the identical line under that gate and builds
    clean.

selectors 0.24.0
    `build.rs` writes a `phf` set to
    `$OUT_DIR/ascii_case_insensitive_html_attributes.rs` and `parser.rs:2051`
    include!s it. Same shape as cssparser's `tokenizer.rs`.

WHY `allow_unsafe` IS SPELLED OUT FOR ALL THREE

Not a claim added by this patch. `fill_allow_unsafe_settings` computes these
three values as `true` on its own and writes them into this file on the first
`gnrt vendor` of a fresh tree; each crate does contain `unsafe` its detector
finds -- cssparser in `src/cow_rc_str.rs`, rmp in `src/encode/buffer.rs`, and
selectors in `builder.rs`, `bloom.rs` and `tree.rs` at the crate root. Declaring
them here changes no value: the vendoring run finds the key present and leaves
it alone.

HOW THE REST OF THE DEPENDENCY SET WAS CHECKED

A round trip per crate is a poor way to find these, so the whole 103-crate
`adblock` closure was scanned from `Cargo.lock` for the four shapes -- a
`build.rs` writing into `OUT_DIR`, a `#[path]` module in a `build.rs`, an
`include_str!`/`include_bytes!` escaping the source directory, and an
`include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), ...))` -- and each hit was cross-checked
against the crate's generated `BUILD.gn`. Eight candidates, of which these
three are real. The other five are doc comments and doctest-gated items
(`phf_codegen`'s `codegen.rs` appears inside a `//!` example, `hashbrown`'s
README behind `#[cfg(doctest)]`, `regex-automata`'s `.dfa` fixtures inside
doc examples), and `thiserror`'s `build/probe.rs`, which its build script
hands to a nested `rustc` rather than reading itself -- an undeclared
incremental-build input, not a failure, and undeclared upstream too.

MEASURED

All three of 064, 065 and 066 applied, `tools/vendor-adblock-rust.sh` re-run,
then from chromium/src with the committed gn_args/linux.gn (verified
byte-identical to out/GateCheck/args.gn):

    $ ./buildtools/linux64/gn gen out/GateCheck
    Done. Made 29957 targets from 4411 files in 9591ms

    $ ./third_party/ninja/ninja -C out/GateCheck -k 0 \
          obj/third_party/rust/cssparser/v0_29/lib/libcssparser_lib.rlib \
          obj/third_party/rust/rmp/v0_8/lib/librmp_lib.rlib \
          obj/third_party/rust/selectors/v0_24/lib/libselectors_lib.rlib
    [11/17] RUST(BIN) .../selectors_lib_v0_24_build_script
    [12/17] ACTION //third_party/rust/selectors/v0_24:selectors_lib_v0_24_build_script_output
    [15/17] RUST obj/third_party/rust/cssparser/v0_29/lib/libcssparser_lib.rlib
    [16/17] RUST obj/third_party/rust/selectors/v0_24/lib/libselectors_lib.rlib
    [3/17]  RUST obj/third_party/rust/rmp/v0_8/lib/librmp_lib.rlib

All three libraries and both build scripts build, from DELETED outputs rather
than from ninja reporting it had nothing to do. The generated files carry the
declarations:

    cssparser/v0_29/BUILD.gn  build_script_inputs = [ ".../src/../build/match_byte.rs" ]
                              build_script_outputs = [ "tokenizer.rs" ]
    rmp/v0_8/BUILD.gn         inputs = [ ".../src/../README.md" ]
    selectors/v0_24/BUILD.gn  build_script_outputs = [ "ascii_case_insensitive_html_attributes.rs" ]

Re-running `tools/vendor-adblock-rust.sh` left `gnrt_config.toml` byte-identical
to what it was before, and all three generated `BUILD.gn` files unchanged.
Byte-identical to the file as it stood, not to what this patch alone produces:
the first vendoring of a fresh tree also auto-fills `allow_unsafe` for every
crate the adblock closure adds that has no key yet. Those entries are gnrt's
own; what is verified here is that none of them displaces these.

The target count is the vacuity floor: a `gn gen` that fails writes no build
graph at all, and every check downstream of one reads clean against nothing.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX, AND WHY IT CANNOT BE FIXED HERE

`//chrome/browser/oxy/adblock/rs:adblock_engine_ffi` still does not link. With
cssparser, rmp and selectors declared, the next thing in the graph fails:

    FAILED: obj/third_party/rust/rmp_serde/v0_15/lib/librmp_serde_lib.rlib
    error[E0425]: cannot find function `read_data_i8` in module `rmp::decode`
    error: aborting due to 24 previous errors

Not a declaration gap and not reachable from `gnrt_config.toml`. rmp-serde
0.15.5 calls `rmp::decode::read_data_*` as FREE functions; rmp 0.8.11 moved them
into the `RmpRead` trait, `#[doc(hidden)]`, and left no free wrappers. Confirmed
against the crates rather than inferred: rmp 0.8.10 `src/decode/mod.rs:208` has
`pub fn read_data_u8<R: Read>(rd: &mut R)`; 0.8.11 `src/decode/mod.rs:86,108`
has `pub trait RmpRead` with `fn read_data_u8(&mut self)` inside it. adblock
0.9.8 requires `rmp-serde = "0.15"` NON-optionally (it is the `data_format`
serializer, not a feature), rmp-serde 0.15.5 requires `rmp = "0.8.8"`, and Cargo
resolves that caret to 0.8.15.

That is not this patch's to fix, and the two repairs named here when it was
written are both wrong. Corrected by 069, which measured them:

  * "An adblock revision on a newer rmp-serde" does not exist below adblock
    0.12.1, the first release that drops rmp-serde altogether. Every release
    from 0.9.8 to 0.12.0 declares `rmp-serde = "^0.15"`, and 0.15.5 is the
    last 0.15.x.
  * "Editing the vendored crate is not an option; the next `gnrt vendor`
    overwrites it silently" is true of editing the tree by hand and false of
    the mechanism. `chromium_crates_io/patches/<crate>-<epoch>/` exists so an
    edit SURVIVES re-vendoring -- `apply_patches` in
    `tools/crates/gnrt/vendor.rs` runs it on every download, and 17 crates in
    this checkout already rely on it. That is the route 069 takes.

Worth carrying for whoever revisits the third option: holding `rmp` below
0.8.11 would falsify the `[crate.rmp]` entry THIS patch adds. The README is a
compile input because 0.8.15's `src/lib.rs` opens
`#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`; 0.8.10's does not.

diff --git a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml
--- a/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml
+++ b/third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/gnrt_config.toml
@@ -203,6 +203,15 @@ allow_unsafe = false
 [crate.crc32fast.extra_kv]
 allow_unsafe = true
 
+# Astro: `build.rs` reaches outside itself in both directions and gnrt cannot
+# see either half. It pulls in `build/match_byte.rs` with a `#[path]` module
+# declaration, and it writes `$OUT_DIR/tokenizer.rs`, which `src/lib.rs`
+# include!s. Neither appears in the generated `BUILD.gn` unless declared.
+[crate.cssparser]
+extra_build_script_src_roots = ['../build']
+build_script_outputs = ['tokenizer.rs']
+extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = true }
+
 [crate.cxx]
 extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = true }
 remove_deps = ['cc', 'link-cplusplus']
@@ -580,6 +589,13 @@ allow_unsafe = false
 [crate.resb.extra_kv]
 allow_unsafe = true
 
+# Astro: `src/lib.rs` opens with `#![doc = include_str!("../README.md")]`, so
+# the README is a compile input. Same declaration upstream already makes for
+# `image`, `prost`, `clap` and `typed-path`.
+[crate.rmp]
+extra_input_roots = ['../README.md']
+extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = true }
+
 [crate.rustc-demangle.extra_kv]
 allow_unsafe = false
 
@@ -598,6 +614,13 @@ allow_unsafe = true
 [crate.scopeguard]
 extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = true }
 
+# Astro: `build.rs` writes a phf set to
+# `$OUT_DIR/ascii_case_insensitive_html_attributes.rs` and `parser.rs`
+# include!s it. Same shape as `cssparser` above.
+[crate.selectors]
+build_script_outputs = ['ascii_case_insensitive_html_attributes.rs']
+extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = true }
+
 [crate.serde]
 build_script_outputs = [ "private.rs" ]
 extra_kv = { allow_unsafe = false }
